# Cloudflare `_redirects` — keeps non-app files out of the public site.
#
# The deploy uploads the whole repository, so every file in it is fetchable.
# That was serving the complete source of all three edge functions
# (bobcat-bites.com/supabase/functions/stripe/index.ts returned 25 KB of
# TypeScript with a 200), plus the MCP config and the setup notes. No secrets
# were in any of them — every credential comes from an environment variable —
# but publishing the implementation hands over the rate-limit thresholds, the
# admin lockout policy and the whole webhook flow for free.
#
# Rules are matched top-down, first match wins, and `404` serves the named page
# with a real 404 status. Anything the students' apps actually load is listed
# nowhere here, so it keeps being served normally.

# Edge function sources. Nothing in the browser ever loads these — the apps call
# the deployed functions on supabase.co, not these files.
/supabase/*        /404.html  404

# Agent + tooling config that ships in the repo for local development.
/.mcp.json         /404.html  404
/.claude/*         /404.html  404
/.agents/*         /404.html  404
/skills-lock.json  /404.html  404
/.gitignore        /404.html  404

# Project documentation, and the Netlify config the site no longer uses.
/README.md         /404.html  404
/STRIPE-SETUP.md   /404.html  404
/netlify.toml      /404.html  404
/BOBCAT_1.pdf      /404.html  404
